[Music]  what's up guys rip and mark man here at  the playstation competition center to  bring you some tips on tekken 7.  today we're going to talk about one of  the most important aspects of attacking  in tekken attack heights  virtually all attacks in tekken fall  under three main heights high attacks  mid attacks and low attacks if you want  to check out which height a certain  attack is  jump into training mode and turn on hit  properties in the display settings  section the differences are not just  cosmetic  each attack serves a specific purpose in  your offensive arsenal  to understand how to use these attacks  we must first learn how blocking works  in tekken 7.  characters can be standing up or  crouching when standing up you will  block both high and mid attacks but low  attacks will hit you  when crouching you will block low  attacks but mid-attack will hit you and  high attacks will just miss over your  head entirely  so the first obvious question is if high  attacks either get blocked or missed  entirely why use them at all  why not just use only mids or lows which  lead to damage if the defender blocks  incorrectly  well let's first talk about mid attacks  many powerful fast combo starters like  uppercuts and hopkicks are mid attacks  so if you crouch block often you risk  getting hit by these launchers and  losing a lot of health very quickly  also the faster low attacks in tekken 7  often do very small amounts of damage  and don't lead to combos  the stronger low attacks tend to be  slower and with some practice you will  learn to react and block them in time  so this means in tekken 7 it's generally  a better idea to block standing more  often than crouching  and that's what makes high attacks very  practical even though they whiff against  crouching opponents  most players will prefer to stand and  avoid those dangerous mid attacks  many useful moves in tekken 7 are high  attacks these useful high attacks often  let you continue your momentum  even if your opponent has blocked them  so they are great for maintaining your  offense  and if your opponent notices this and  starts to crouch more bring out your  most dangerous mid attack to show them  why they shouldn't duck  of course if you're standing the entire  time your opponent may attack you with a  lot of small damage but annoying low  attack  and over time you're gonna lose quite a  bit of light so how do you handle those  two  all those in tekken 7 come with the  universal weakness every character in  the game can carry low attack by tapping  and holding the down forward direction  on the controller  if the enemy attack is low in doing this  you automatically knock them down  and can land a follow-up combo so now  you're on the offense instead  so if an opponent attacks too often with  loads low pairing is a great way to turn  the tide  as you can see there's a nice balance  between the different attack heights the  high the mid and the low  by standing there you'll be able to  block very damaging and dangerous mid  attacks but you're also forced to block  these high attacks and you might need  some low attacks  alternatively if you're ducking you put  yourself at a huge risk and you might  eat a mid-launcher  right and even if you just learn one or  two attacks from each of these hit  ranges you know it's really enough to  keep your opponent guessing  that's it for this episode this tutorial  is made in partnership with the  playstation competition center team  you can check out compete.playstation to  watch  learn and compete subscribe to the bne  esports channel for more tutorials  and tekken 7 content

